review(2168,[on],'Dewdrop names her motorcycle sprites the Pixie Dusters.', ['The script explicitly names her gang Pixie Dusters.','Wing Clippers is not the gang name in Dewdrop call.','Fairy Riders is not the gang name in Dewdrop call.','Sprite Squad is not the gang name in Dewdrop call.'],'Disused wings do not imply permanent flight loss; final wording asks only the unique named gang.','Onward (2020), Dewdrop motorcycle sprites.','Distinct from the town, magic, tavern and unicorn behavior questions.')
review(2169,[on],'The expressway alternative is the named Path of Peril.', ['Barley proposes this trail by name.','Shadow Trail differs from the spoken route name.','Serpent Pass differs from the spoken route name.','Old Elf Road differs from the spoken route name.'],'The route is not asserted to be shorter or faster; exclude the other three by the named expressway discussion.','Onward (2020), route argument.','New route name, not the quest gift or van identity.')
review(2170,[oncast],'D23 explicitly credits Laurel to Julia Louis-Dreyfus.', ['She holds the specified original English voice credit.','Tina Fey voices 22 in Soul, not this role.','Allison Janney is not the actress credited for Laurel.','Melissa McCarthy is not the actress credited for Laurel.'],'Language is fixed; fame or other animation roles cannot substitute for the unique Laurel credit.','Original English Onward (2020).','Mother identity 1559 and Laurel actress require different facts; Soul cast comparisons concern other roles.')
review(2171,[onfather],'Scanlon directly identifies his early loss of his father as the story inspiration.', ['He says his father died when he was about one.','The cited inspiration is bereavement, not parental divorce.','He describes his brother as alive and sharing the recording, not a brother death.','His stated formative loss is his father, not a house fire.'],'This is a specifically attributed inspiration, not a claim that no other childhood event occurred.','Dan Scanlon account of Onward development.','Different from in-world father visitation magic and plot questions.')
review(2172,[lucacat],'Pixar identifies Giulia cat as Machiavelli.', ['Machiavelli is the named pet cat.','Ravioli is not the name in the cat profile.','Vespa is the scooter brand, not this cat.','Napoleone is not the name in the cat profile.'],'The singular named pet, not any Italian name, determines the answer; the fish-sensing premise is explicit.','Luca (2021), Giulia household.','No other cat-name question for this character in the full topic context.')
review(2173,[lucarace],'The trio adopts Underdogs and the race announcer uses it.', ['Underdogs is the team agreed upon and announced.','Sea Devils is not the named team.','Team Portorosso confuses the town/race with the trio name.','Speedsters is not the named team.'],'Race under supplies no dog clue; both team agreement and announcement establish the exact group name.','Luca (2021), Cup team.','Different from race name 1043 and race events 1440.')
review(2174,[luca,luvaspa],'Vespa is the scooter brand the boys want to buy.', ['The scooter dream and poster explicitly identify Vespa.','Lambretta is a different scooter brand, not the boys goal.','Piaggio Ape is not the Vespa they seek.','Vespino is not the brand named for their goal.'],'Replaced specific model with brand; a corporate relationship between Piaggio and Vespa does not make an Ape a Vespa scooter.','Luca (2021), scooter dream.','Distinct from the Cup name/events and Alberto tower.')
review(2175,[luca],'Alberto mantra uses the name Bruno to silence fear.', ['Silenzio, Bruno is the explicitly discussed mantra.','Andiamo, Luca is not the supplied mantra.','Coraggio, amico is not the supplied mantra.','Bene, bene is not the supplied mantra.'],'Other encouraging Italian phrases are not interchangeable with the exact phrase he teaches.','Original dialogue of Luca (2021).','New mantra, not Giulia astronomy lesson or Cup details.')
review(2176,[luca],'Casarosa biography names La Luna as his earlier directorial short.', ['La Luna is the short credited to Casarosa.','Piper is Alan Barillaro short, not Casarosa.','Geri Game is Jan Pinkava short, not Casarosa.','Bao is Domee Shi short, not Casarosa.'],'Removed unnecessary first/sole feature claim. The specific short-director credit excludes the alternatives.','Casarosa career before Luca (2021).','Distinct director credit; no duplication of Luca setting or other shorts story facts.')
review(2177,[cocoshoes],'The Rivera family business is making shoes.', ['Shoemaking is the explicitly named family trade.','Weaving is not the identified multigeneration family business.','Baking is not the identified multigeneration family business.','Pottery is not the identified multigeneration family business.'],'Family musical talent does not make another listed craft their business; the profile expressly names shoemaking.','Coco (2017), Rivera family trade.','Distinct from Imelda music ban and family relationship questions.')
review(2178,[cocoscript,cocoscene],'Héctor claims he is Frida at the checkpoint and admits it is a lie.', ['Frida Kahlo is the explicit impersonation.','A mariachi is not the identity claimed at this checkpoint.','A police officer is not the identity claimed at this checkpoint.','Ernesto is not the identity claimed at this checkpoint.'],'He fails to cross; the final stem asks an attempt. His later performance costumes cannot replace this checkpoint disguise.','Coco (2017), bridge checkpoint.','2055 asks the real artist cameo; knowing the artist appears does not establish Héctor impersonates her.')
review(2179,[cocoscript,cocoscene,cocoplot],'The reveal identifies murder by poison before Ernesto appropriates Héctor music.', ['Ernesto poisons Héctor.','The reveal is murder, not a contractual transfer of rights.','The reveal does not substitute publisher bribery for the poisoning.','Héctor death is caused by poison, not natural causes.'],'Distinguished the early food-poisoning belief from deliberate poisoning in the reveal; all options now describe alternative acts.','Coco (2017), Ernesto confrontation/reveal.','A new murder mechanism, not the musician idol name or guitar location.')
review(2180,[cocoscene,cocoplot],'The family blessing must happen by sunrise or Miguel stays in the dead world.', ['The stated permanent consequence is remaining in the Land of the Dead.','Returning without memories contradicts remaining there.','Returning aged contradicts remaining there.','Returning unable to play music contradicts remaining there.'],'All three wrong choices require a return, so none can coexist with the stated consequence of missing the deadline.','Coco (2017), curse deadline.','Separate from final death of forgotten skeletons and photo crossing rule.')
review(2181,[up],'The lead dog addresses his two subordinates Beta and Gamma.', ['Alpha, Beta and Gamma are the three dogs in the script.','Rex/Fido/Duke does not match the named trio.','Max/Zeus/Apollo does not match the named trio.','Bruno/Diesel/Rocco does not match the named trio.'],'It is the specified trio, not all of Muntz dogs; Dug is not silently included as a fourth answer.','Up (2009), Muntz lead dogs.','Separate from Dug breed/collar and the squirrel distraction.')
review(2182,[up],'The newsreel and later cave scene name the airship Spirit of Adventure.', ['Spirit of Adventure is the explicitly named dirigible.','Wandering Explorer is a different, unspoken name.','Sky Voyager is a different, unspoken name.','Adventure Seeker is a different, unspoken name.'],'The house is another flying dwelling, but the question specifies Muntz airship; no duration claim remains.','Up (2009), Muntz dirigible.','Distinct from villain identity, Paradise Falls and Carl house balloons.')
review(2183,[up],'Ellie final written message encourages Carl to have another adventure.', ['Having a new adventure accurately conveys the note.','Staying home preserving belongings reverses its message.','Returning the house to their street is not its instruction.','Abandoning Russell is not its instruction; Carl takes up his sash afterward.'],'Adventure Book title identifies the object, not the message; all four choices are actions and the note directly distinguishes moving forward.','Up (2009), final filled Adventure Book pages.','Different from Ellie identity, life montage music and Paradise Falls destination.')
review(2184,[up],'The ending explicitly shows Carl and Russell licking ice-cream cones.', ['Ice cream is the treat named in the final scene.','Popcorn is not the treat in their hands at Fentons.','Cotton candy is not the treat in their hands at Fentons.','Soda floats are not the cones described in the ending.'],'The specified curb ending matches Russell earlier father memory; other treats elsewhere cannot answer it.','Up (2009), Fentons final scene.','New ending food detail, not balloon-selling job or assisting badge.')
review(2185,[cinder,cinderreview],'The first royal-duties segment is Aim to Please.', ['Aim to Please names the first segment.','Tall Tail is the second Jaq story.','An Uncommon Romance is the third Anastasia story.','A Royal Welcome is not one of the three listed segment titles.'],'All titles are presented as possible segment names; the complete three-story list excludes the invented title.','Cinderella II: Dreams Come True (2002), segment order.','Segment identity differs from particular banquet responsibility 2188 and Jaq transformation 2186.')
review(2186,[cinder,cinderdialogue],'The Fairy Godmother grants Jaq wish to become human.', ['Jaq is named while the spell and human greeting occur.','Gus remains a mouse and is not this transformed figure.','Suzy is not the named recipient of the spell.','Perla is not the named recipient of the spell.'],'The transformation is specific to Tall Tail, not the original carriage magic; the dialogue repeatedly names human Jaq.','Cinderella II (2002), Tall Tail.','Separate from original two-mouse names and Jaq fear of the cat.')
review(2187,[cinderdialogue,cinder],'Human Jaq names Pom Pom and says he remains afraid of the cat.', ['Pom-Pom is the cat he explicitly fears in this passage.','Bruno is a dog and not the cat he names.','Major is a horse and not the cat he names.','Lucifer is the other household cat, not Pom-Pom in this palace passage.'],'Removed the uncertain motive that the cat fails to recognize him; Jaq fear itself is explicit regardless of whether a chase occurs.','Cinderella II (2002), human Jaq at the palace.','Different from original Lucifer pet identity and mouse-to-human spell recipient.')
review(2188,[cinderdialogue,cinder],'The King assigns Cinderella the royal banquet before leaving with the Prince.', ['The banquet is explicitly Cinderella responsibility.','A treasury inspection is not the event assigned in the departure scene.','Their wedding has already happened, before the honeymoon.','A coronation is not the event assigned in this scene.'],'A spring festival in the next segment is a different event; the full film title and Aim to Please context prevent conflation.','Cinderella II (2002), Aim to Please.','Different from naming the segment: this asks the specific assignment.')
review(2189,[jafar,jafarplot],'Abis Mal retrieves the lamp from the well and releases Jafar.', ['Abis Mal is named when he discovers and rubs the lamp.','Iago puts the lamp into the well rather than becoming its new master.','The Sultan is not the well discoverer.','Razoul is not the well discoverer.'],'Distinguished disposal by Iago from retrieval by Abis Mal and later lamp destruction.','The Return of Jafar (1994), well scene.','2013 asks Iago destruction of the lamp, a different action and time.')
review(2190,[jafar,jafarplot],'Freed Genie retains magic but explicitly describes diminished powers.', ['Less powerful matches his own description and plot account.','More powerful reverses the comparison.','Completely gone conflicts with his demonstrated remaining magic.','Transferred to Iago conflicts with Genie retaining and using magic.'],'Freedom limits strength; the final stem avoids asserting travel itself depleted his powers.','The Return of Jafar (1994), Genie return.','Distinct from original film wish-granting restrictions.')
review(2191,[jafar,jafarplot],'The Sultan explicitly offers royal vizier at dinner.', ['Royal vizier is the spoken title.','Royal wizard is not the offered title.','Head of the guard is not the offered title.','Palace treasurer is not the offered title.'],'Court advisor was also defensible and was replaced; later Aladdin refusal does not invalidate the earlier offer.','The Return of Jafar (1994), palace dinner offer.','Different from Jafar lamp master and framing disguise.')
review(2192,[jafar,jafarplot],'The false Jasmine accusation is Jafar shapeshifting.', ['Princess Jasmine is the identity he assumes during the accusation.','The Sultan is the supposed victim, not the accusing impersonation.','Genie is imprisoned and not the accusing disguise.','Abis Mal assists Jafar but is not the accusing disguise.'],'Jafar uses other transformations elsewhere; only the Sultan-murder accusation/execution sequence is asked.','The Return of Jafar (1994), framing of Aladdin.','Separate new disguise fact from lamp discovery and Iago destruction.')
review(2193,[bear,beardialogue],'Atka is the named groom at the interrupted ceremony.', ['Atka is the intended bridegroom.','Denahi is Kenai brother, not the groom.','Innoko is the shaman, not the groom.','Koda is the bear cub, not the groom.'],'Nita later chooses Kenai, but the stem fixes the initial wedding before the Spirits intervene.','Brother Bear 2 (2006), initial wedding.','Distinct from Kenai childhood friendship and amulet destruction.')
review(2194,[bear,beardialogue],'The adviser who explains the amulet bond is Innoko.', ['Innoko is identified as the consulting shaman.','Tanana belongs to Kenai original-film spiritual guidance, not this consultation.','Denahi is Kenai brother, not the shaman.','Sitka is Kenai deceased elder brother, not this shaman.'],'Separated the sequel consultation from the first film Tanana; no shared generic shaman label suffices.','Brother Bear 2 (2006), Nita consultation.','2050 asks what to burn; this asks the person who explains the bond.')
