review(2199,[kronk,kronkcor],'Both inspected reviews name visiting father Papi.', ['Papi is the visiting father name.','Pacha is Kronk friend, not his father.','Bucky is the squirrel, not his father.','Yzma is his former employer, not his father.'],'A familiar use of papi as father does not make another character his father; the role is explicitly named in both accounts.','Kronk New Groove (2005), father visit.','2098 asks what home/family success he pretends to have, not the father name.')
review(2200,[kronk,kronkcor],'Yzma markets a phony youth-restoring potion to the seniors.', ['Youth restoration is the advertised claim.','Hiccup relief is not the advertised purpose.','Memory improvement is not the advertised purpose.','Strength enhancement is not the advertised purpose.'],'The question asks the sales claim, not whether the potion actually works; food products were removed as weak alternatives.','Kronk New Groove (2005), Yzma scam flashback.','The prior product duplicate 2099 is already retired; unrelated spinach-puff identity 1080 is a different fact.')
review(2201,[kronk,kronkcor],'The romance is strained by rival camp teams competing for the Junior Chipmunk championship.', ['The Junior Chipmunk team rivalry is the conflict described.','Competing restaurants are not their rivalry.','Their mutual baking interest is not a competing cooking contest.','Competing delivery routes are not their rivalry.'],'Cooking brings them closer, while the team championship drives the dispute; the correct activity is independently described in both reviews.','Kronk New Groove (2005), camp flashback.','New activity/conflict fact, separate from father wish and potion scam.')
review(2202,[bambi,bambicor],'The pre-Mena father/son play is mock stag combat with headbutting.', ['Headbutting is the described sparring practice.','Running fast is not the mock stag-combat action asked here.','Jumping over logs belongs to other practice scenes, not this pre-Mena playfight.','Swimming is not the described forest playfight.'],'Removed the unsupported failed-lesson/bouncing embellishment; the narrowed scene is the rival-stag play just before Owl introduction.','Bambi II (2006), morning forest play before Mena.','Different from 2203 exact raspberry action; this is Bambi sparring practice.')
review(2203,[bambi,bambicor],'The sound cue and detailed scene account identify a raspberry on Bambi belly.', ['Both the scene account and sound caption identify a raspberry.','Grooming is not the action identified by the raspberry cue.','Checking for thorns is not the action identified by the raspberry cue.','Brushing off snow is not the action identified by the raspberry cue.'],'A raspberry can tickle, so tickle was removed as an overlapping alternative; the precise interrupted action now has one answer.','Bambi II (2006), Owl interrupts father/son play.','2202 asks headbutting practice, not the father belly gesture.')
review(2204,[fever,feverofficial],'Elsa names Kristoff when delegating responsibility for the courtyard.', ['Kristoff is directly addressed in her question about leaving him in charge.','Olaf helps but is addressed over eating cake, not this delegation.','Sven helps but is not the named addressee.','The Duke is not part of this named delegation.'],'Helping guard is not equivalent to being explicitly asked to take charge; final wording resolves the multiple-helper ambiguity.','Frozen Fever (2015), opening courtyard.','232 asks his original-film occupation/role, a different fact.')
review(2205,[feverofficial],'The D23 filmmaker interview announces the short before Cinderella in March 2015.', ['Cinderella is the companion feature explicitly announced.','Tomorrowland is a different Disney feature, not this pairing.','Into the Woods is a different Disney feature, not this pairing.','Maleficent is a different Disney feature, not this pairing.'],'All four are live-action Disney releases so format gives no answer; pairing, not release year alone, is needed.','Initial 2015 theatrical release of Frozen Fever.','1188 concerns the 1950 animated Cinderella historical role, not the 2015 short pairing.')
review(2206,[olaf],'The opening identifies the Jule Bell with Kristoff and Sven and explains its holiday signal.', ['Jule Bell is explicitly named as their arrival item.','A town clock is not the named object.','A giant snowflake is not the named object.','A chandelier is not the named object.'],'The named opening bell is distinguished from later bells used to gather searchers; it is not an arbitrary large decoration.','Olaf Frozen Adventure (2017), opening holiday ceremony.','Separate from holiday-tradition search motive and Norway cookie.')
review(2207,[olaf,olafcor],'The traditions are loaded into the sleigh for return to the castle.', ['The identified transport is Kristoff sleigh.','Riding Sven back is different from loading the sleigh Sven pulls.','A rowboat is not the loaded return vehicle.','Marshmallow shoulders are not the loaded return vehicle.'],'The revision avoids claiming Olaf rides to every door; Sven draws the vehicle rather than being the answer himself.','Olaf Frozen Adventure (2017), collection and return.','Different from why Olaf collects traditions and the opening Jule Bell.')
review(2208,[geri,gericor],'The winner is handed dentures as the match prize.', ['Dentures are explicitly handed over as the prize.','Glasses distinguish a persona but are not the prize.','A coat is not the item surrendered.','The chess set is used for the match but is not the prize.'],'Removed the reversed Black-wins-from-White premise; the question is now only the witnessed prize transfer.','Geri Game (1997), ending.','2078 asks which game; 2324 asks the winning trick, not the prize. Its mistaken identity is separately flagged.')
review(2209,[piper],'Pixar explicitly identifies its hatchling as a sandpiper.', ['Sandpiper is the bird identified in the studio synopsis.','A seagull is a different bird.','A pelican is a different bird.','A plover is another shorebird, not the identified sandpiper.'],'The near-plausible plover does not override Pixar species identification; the title wordplay is not the sole evidence.','Piper (2016), title hatchling.','2327 concerns technique learned from crab; 2328 aquarium research; 2329 companion feature.')
review(2210,[bao,baocor],'Domee Shi directly explains that the mother eats the dumpling to stop him leaving.', ['Eating him is the filmmaker stated twist.','Locking him in his room is not that final act.','Calling off the wedding is not that final act.','Running away is not that final act.'],'This asks the metaphorical dumpling sequence, not literal cannibalism of her real son; the fiancée detail fixes the scene.','Bao (2018), allegorical dumpling-son sequence.','2080 asks what comes alive; this asks the later maternal action.')
review(2211,[baocity,baocor],'The setting is Toronto, corroborated by its CN Tower and streetcars.', ['Toronto is explicitly identified as the setting.','Vancouver is a different Canadian city, not this setting.','Chicago is not the city identified.','San Francisco is the studio-region association, not the story setting.'],'Chinese-Canadian does not by itself select Toronto over Vancouver; the setting evidence and landmarks do.','Bao (2018), family city.','1401 asks Turning Red setting; knowing one film city does not establish the other film city.')
review(2212,[imagination,imaginationcor],'Dreamfinder is the original human host with Figment.', ['Dreamfinder is the host identified with Figment.','Wayne Szalinski belongs to the later Imagination presentation, not this original human host.','Merlin is not the original ride host.','The Imagineer is not the named original ride host.'],'Removed accidental creation and redundant year; the original incarnation excludes later hosts.','Original EPCOT Journey Into Imagination.','1140 asks Figment identity; this asks his human companion.')
review(2213,[imagination],'Kodak sponsorship begins with the pavilion in 1982, before its ride opened.', ['Kodak is the named original sponsor.','Polaroid is a different company, not the original sponsor.','Fujifilm is a different company, not the original sponsor.','Canon is a different company, not the original sponsor.'],'Corrected 1983 to 1982 for the pavilion; the ride date cannot be used as the pavilion date.','EPCOT pavilion opening in 1982.','Different from 2214 ride opening year and 2212 host.')
review(2214,[imagination,imaginationcor],'Both official histories date the ride opening to March 5, 1983.', ['1983 is the ride opening year.','1971 is not the documented opening year.','1989 is not the documented opening year.','1994 is not the documented opening year.'],'Explicitly asks ride, not pavilion or EPCOT park; the date is confirmed by two Disney history entries.','Original EPCOT ride opening.','97 asks EPCOT park opening in 1982, not this attraction opening.')
review(2215,[cocopark,cocoparkcor],'The historical PhilharMagic update added Un Poco Loco.', ['Un Poco Loco is the identified new scene number.','Remember Me is another Coco song, not the added scene number.','Proud Corazon is another Coco song, not the added scene number.','The World Es Mi Familia is another Coco song, not the added scene number.'],'A historical update avoids assuming current lineup; the official announcement and completed-update account agree.','Magic Kingdom 2021 PhilharMagic update.','2287 identifies the song in a Coco plaza scene/translation; the attraction addition requires a new fact.')
review(2216,[track,trackcor],'The December 2012 redesign uses the Chevrolet brand.', ['Chevrolet is named on the design center and attraction signage.','Ford is not the brand of that redesign.','Toyota is not the brand of that redesign.','Honda is not the brand of that redesign.'],'The original and later GM branding do not change the specifically dated Chevrolet edition; no current sponsor assertion remains.','EPCOT Test Track December 2012 edition.','356 concerns original attraction opening/identity, not redesign branding.')
review(2217,[speed],'Disney historical account advertises up to 65 mph for the original ride.', ['65 mph matches the historical advertised approximate maximum.','45 mph is below the specified advertised maximum.','80 mph exceeds the specified advertised maximum.','100 mph exceeds the specified advertised maximum.'],'About allows minor measured/readout rounding; the stem asks advertised historical maximum rather than every ride actual speed.','Original Test Track opened in 1999, before 2012 remodeling.','Separate from Test Track identity/opening and Chevrolet redesign.')

library['sources'].update(sources)
write('audit/source-notes.json',library)
notes=read('audit/runs/next-shard-0033-final-template.json')
notes['sourcesChecked']=sorted(set(s for row in rows.values() for s in row[0]))
allchecks=['singleAnswer','context','wording','noGiveaway','distinctFact','category','difficulty','scope']
out=[]
for r in notes['reviews']:
    i=r['questionId']
    if i==2196:continue
    ss,premise,reasons,challenge,context,distinct=rows[i]
    r.update(checks=allchecks,notes=distinct+' All four final options assessed; category and difficulty checked. Secondary films/shorts remain within the approximate 8–10-title soft cap where applicable.',context=context,timeSensitive=False,nextReviewAt=None)
    r['premise']={'reason':premise,'sources':ss}
    r['options']=[{'basis':'direct' if n==0 else 'exclusive-inference','reason':why,'sources':ss} for n,why in enumerate(reasons)]
    r['challenge']={'reviewer':'Codex','at':'2026-11-09','premiseChecked':True,'alternativesExcluded':True,'notes':challenge}
    out.append(r)
notes['reviews']=out
assert len(out)==49 and set(rows)=={r['questionId'] for r in out}
write('audit/runs/next-shard-0033-reviewed-notes.json',notes)
print('Authored 49 full final-wording reviews and',len(sources),'passage-specific source notes.')
